# Implementation Plan - CPIS Phase 3: LangGraph Agentic Parser & Matcher

This document outlines the design and implementation details for Phase 3 of the Career Pipeline Intelligence System (CPIS) — the **LangGraph Agentic Resume Extraction, Validation, Self-Correction, and Job Matching Layer**.

## User Review Required

We are building a stateful, cyclic multi-agent system using LangGraph that processes ingested candidate resumes. The system will perform:
1. **Structured LLM Extraction**: Feed clean resume text to the Gemini API to extract structured fields conforming to a robust Pydantic schema.
2. **Self-Correction Loop**: Validate the extracted fields against business rules (e.g., presence of candidate name, valid email, non-empty skills). If validation fails, loop back to the extraction node with details of the validation errors so the model can self-correct, up to a configurable max revision limit.
3. **Semantic Job Matching**: Search ChromaDB vector store for matching jobs using candidate skills and experience context, evaluating fit scores.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **API Key dependency & Mocking**
> - Production execution requires a valid `GEMINI_API_KEY`.
> - For unit/integration tests and offline development, we will design the agent layer to support mock LLM responses. This guarantees that test suites run successfully in any environment.

## Open Questions

None. We will implement robust schemas and prompts following best practices, keeping all variables configurable via settings.

